# shell: desktop
# PVL-032/IV-024: a list row IS its columns.  This shell drew a name and one
# right-aligned value, so every column the title strip offered was a heading
# over an empty strip -- and the selection ran the width of the row.
wait 6
expect-columns 4
note the Kind column's cells carry text.  The strip starts at x 329 (the
note heading is drawn there) and the first row's text sits at y 116.
expect-ink 338 116
expect-ink 350 120
note and selecting a row lights the icon and the NAME column only: past the
note name, the row keeps the document ground
click-row 0
wait 4
expect-pixel 300 118 336698
expect-pixel 400 118 ffffff
note and the window as a whole is what a full redraw would draw
expect-same-as-redraw
quit
